sepolicy: let the MatonOS Flatpak sandbox domain execute its own app data

Adds the private attribute data_exec_exempt_domain and exempts it from the
two domain.te neverallows that forbid non-app domains executing data files
(execute only exec/system/vendor files; no execute of data_file_type).
Nothing in AOSP carries the attribute.
MatonOS gives it only to matonos_linux_app: Linux/Flatpak app sandboxes,
which may run code downloaded into their own app data (as on a Linux
desktop). That domain is not an appdomain (appdomains can only be entered
from zygote and may hold no capabilities) and has no binder. Every other
domain keeps W^X. See install/linuxd/CODE-STORAGE-r24.md.

MatonOS: user-approved second patch-budget entry (2026-10-04).

diff --git a/private/attributes b/private/attributes
index d0c07e0e5..8ee9287af 100644
--- a/private/attributes
+++ b/private/attributes
@@ -27,3 +27,9 @@ expandattribute update_provider false;
 # of the OMAPI services. Remove once the RELEASE_NATIVE_OMAPI flag is cleaned
 # up and the app-based implementation is removed.
 attribute omapi_server;
+
+# MatonOS: non-app domains that may execute their own app data
+# (Linux/Flatpak sandboxes, matonos_linux_app). Exempts them
+# from the two domain.te neverallows that forbid non-app domains executing
+# data files. Nothing in AOSP carries this attribute.
+attribute data_exec_exempt_domain;
diff --git a/private/domain.te b/private/domain.te
index 248a42f62..2fca67364 100644
--- a/private/domain.te
+++ b/private/domain.te
@@ -1970,6 +1970,7 @@ neverallow {
     userdebug_or_eng(`-mediaextractor')
     userdebug_or_eng(`-mediaswcodec')
     userdebug_or_eng(`-overlay_remounter')
+    -data_exec_exempt_domain
 } {
     file_type
     -system_file_type
@@ -2042,6 +2043,7 @@ neverallow {
   domain
   -appdomain
   userdebug_or_eng(`-overlay_remounter')
+  -data_exec_exempt_domain
 } {
   data_file_type
   -apex_art_data_file
